      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{xy-z},$ find the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ exists.",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)$ is defined only when \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy-z & \\ge 0 \\\\ xy & \\ge z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge z\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivative of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xy-z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xy-z}}\\cdot x \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy-z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{y}(x,y,z)$ is defined only for \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy-z & >0 \\\\ xy & >z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>z\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge z\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>z\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>z\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
